  "language": "en",
  "text": "ordinarium.praefatio-d-n-iesu-christi-regis",
  "about": "The Preface of Christ the King. It praises Christ's eternal priesthood and universal kingship and the kingdom of truth, life, holiness, grace, justice, love, and peace.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": {
      "narrative": "Then the priest separates his hands and holds them apart until the end of the Preface. When it is finished, he joins them again and, bowing, says: Sanctus."
    },
    "s02": {
      "translation": "It is truly meet and just, right and profitable for salvation, that we should at all times and in all places give thanks unto Thee:"
    },
    "s03": {
      "translation": "O Lord, holy Father, almighty eternal God:"
    },
    "s04": {
      "translation": "Who didst anoint with the oil of gladness Thine only-begotten Son, our Lord Jesus Christ, eternal Priest and King of all, that offering Himself upon the altar of the Cross as a spotless and peace-giving Victim, He might accomplish the mysteries of mankind's redemption; and that, all creatures having been subjected to His dominion, He might deliver to Thine infinite Majesty an eternal and universal kingdom: a kingdom of truth and life, a kingdom of holiness and grace, a kingdom of justice, love, and peace."
    },
    "s05": {
      "translation": "And therefore with Angels and Archangels, with Thrones and Dominions, and with all the hosts of the heavenly army, we sing the hymn of Thy glory, evermore saying:"
    }
  },
